## --- Configuration & Dependencies

### File: `.env`

This file stores environment-specific variables and sensitive data securely. It is crucial for maintaining the flexibility and security of your automation suite.

```dotenv
# Base URL for the application under test
BASE_URL=https://your-application-domain.com

# Example Patient ID for the test case (used in Test DataSets)
TEST_PATIENT_ID=P-001
TEST_PATIENT_NAME=John Doe
TEST_COPAY_AMOUNT=$50.00
TEST_PATIENT_EMAIL=john.doe@example.com
TEST_PAYMENT_PORTAL_LINK=https://payment.example.com/portal/P-001

# --- Sensitive Data & Security ---
# IMPORTANT: DO NOT hardcode sensitive data like passwords or tokens directly in the code.
# Instead, define them here and access them via process.env in envUtils.ts.
# Example:
# API_TOKEN=your_secure_api_token_here
# DATABASE_PASSWORD=your_database_password_here
```

