automationScripts.content:
This is a production-ready, enterprise-grade QA Automation architecture built with **Playwright** and **TypeScript**. 

It implements the **Page Object Model (POM)** pattern, adheres strictly to clean coding practices, secures configuration variables through a unified environment utility, scales dynamically across desktop, tablet, and mobile viewport resolutions, and executes test suites without relying on arbitrary timeouts or unstable selectors.

---

### 📂 Folder Structure

```text
automation-project/
├── .env
├── package.json
├── playwright.config.ts
├── pages/
│   ├── BasePage.ts
│   ├── HomePage.ts
│   ├── ContactUsPage.ts
│   └── SearchResultsPage.ts
├── tests/
│   ├── app.setup.ts
│   ├── navigation.spec.ts
│   ├── search.spec.ts
│   ├── contactUs.spec.ts
│   ├── localization.spec.ts
│   └── responsiveness.spec.ts
└── utils/
    └── envUtils.ts
```

---

### --- Configuration & Dependencies

#### `.env`
```env
# Target Environment Configuration
BASE_URL=https://www.servicenow.com/in/
```

---

#### `utils/envUtils.ts`
```typescript
import * as dotenv from 'dotenv';
import * as path from 'path';

// Resolve environment variables from the root folder
dotenv.config({ path: path.resolve(__dirname, '../.env') });

/**
 * Enterprise Environment Variable Handler
 */
export class EnvUtils {
    public static readonly BASE_URL = process.env.BASE_URL || 'https://www.servicenow.com/in/';
}
```

---

#### `package.json`
```json
{
  "name": "playwright-enterprise-framework",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "Enterprise Playwright TypeScript Automation Framework",
  "main": "index.js",
  "scripts": {
    "clean": "rimraf test-results playwright-report",
    "test": "npx playwright test",
    "test:chromium": "npx playwright test --project=chromium",
    "test:setup": "npx playwright test --project=setup",
    "codegen": "npx playwright codegen"
  },
  "devDependencies": {
    "@playwright/test": "^1.42.1",
    "@types/node": "^20.11.24",
    "dotenv": "^16.4.5",
    "rimraf": "^5.0.5",
    "typescript": "^5.3.3"
  }
}
```

---

#### `playwright.config.ts`
```typescript
import { defineConfig, devices } from '@playwright/test';
import { EnvUtils } from './utils/envUtils';
import * as path from 'path';

// Location where shared context / session states are stored
const STORAGE_STATE = path.join(__dirname, 'playwright/.auth/user.json');

// Generate unique ID per run for reporting structure
const runId = new Date().getTime();

export default defineConfig({
  // Run settings
  fullyParallel: false,
  workers: 1,
  retries: 0,

  // High reliability execution settings
  timeout: 180000,
  expect: {
    timeout: 60000,
  },

  outputDir: 'test-results/run-' + runId,
  reporter: [
    ['html', { outputFolder: 'playwright-report/run-' + runId }]
  ],

  use: {
    baseURL: EnvUtils.BASE_URL,
    actionTimeout: 50000,
    trace: 'on',
    screenshot: 'only-on-failure',
    video: 'retain-on-failure',
  },

  projects: [
    {
      name: 'setup',
      testMatch: /.*.setup.ts/,
    },
    {
      name: 'chromium',
